      "output": "## Castle models: eight files, handed on unchanged\n\nAll eight files were read by one standard-library Python script (`inspect_glb.py`), copied to their own names and published. Each publish receipt's SHA-256 equals the one the script computed and the one supplied with the upload.\n\n| File | Bytes | Meshes | Triangles | Materials | Textures (embedded WebP: colour / ORM / normal, bytes) | Size in metres, X × Y × Z | SHA-256 (first 12) | Same bytes |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|\n| keep-drum-b.glb | 1,083,700 | 1 | 13,062 | 1 | 3 at 2048 px: 396,264 / 124,196 / 277,540 | 0.572 × 0.998 × 0.525 | `da1a9b354d37` | same bytes: yes |\n| long-hall.glb | 1,053,720 | 1 | 13,074 | 1 | 3 at 2048 px: 325,598 / 200,684 / 247,382 | 0.568 × 0.760 × 0.998 | `506dc5b7f656` | same bytes: yes |\n| cloister.glb | 802,652 | 1 | 8,742 | 1 | 3 at 2048 px: 274,230 / 98,698 / 244,502 | 0.381 × 0.475 × 0.998 | `73a2eacede84` | same bytes: yes |\n| bell-tower.glb | 534,516 | 1 | 10,293 | 1 | 3 at 1024 px: 114,770 / 106,358 / 86,852 | 0.225 × 0.998 × 0.225 | `38d4a2b87658` | same bytes: yes |\n| tower-slim.glb | 501,584 | 1 | 8,185 | 1 | 3 at 1024 px: 124,842 / 65,158 / 137,368 | 0.232 × 0.998 × 0.232 | `15e26b90bfaa` | same bytes: yes |\n| tower-stout.glb | 424,872 | 1 | 8,523 | 1 | 3 at 1024 px: 99,284 / 70,950 / 55,136 | 0.725 × 0.998 × 0.686 | `58ade82b0622` | same bytes: yes |\n| wall-curtain.glb | 473,632 | 1 | 4,412 | 1 | 3 at 1024 px: 145,152 / 66,084 / 153,048 | 0.283 × 0.365 × 0.998 | `4d1f1a1b38f7` | same bytes: yes |\n| gatehouse.glb | 419,236 | 1 | 10,884 | 1 | 3 at 1024 px: 78,962 / 63,056 / 56,448 | 0.553 × 0.998 × 0.873 | `1cc7c8ffc1e4` | same bytes: yes |\n\nTotal: 5,293,912 bytes and 77,175 triangles.\n\n**How the figures were read.**\n- **Structure:** every file is glTF 2.0 binary with one JSON chunk and one BIN chunk, and the header length equals the file size. Each has one mesh with one indexed triangle primitive, one node and one scene. None has animations, skins or cameras.\n- **Material:** each file's single material is double-sided and opaque, with colour, metallic-roughness and normal textures.\n- **Compression:** every file lists `EXT_meshopt_compression`, `EXT_texture_webp` and `KHR_mesh_quantization` in both `extensionsUsed` and `extensionsRequired`. There is no Draco.\n- **Size:** this is not the raw accessor box. POSITION min/max are normalised 16-bit integers, so they were divided by 32767 and then passed through each node's scale of 0.4990234375.\n- **Not checked:** the meshopt vertex data was not decoded, because the standard library has no decoder. Triangle counts and sizes are what each file's JSON declares. No model was rendered or loaded in an engine.\n\n**For the builders.**\n- **Loader:** all three extensions are required, so the loader must have a meshopt decoder and WebP texture support. Without them these files will not load.\n- **Scale:** every model is normalised to 0.998 m on its longest axis and centred on the origin. None is at castle scale, and their proportions to one another are not kept: the curtain wall and the keep are both 0.998 m long. The game has to scale and place each one itself.\n- **Long axis:** it is Y (up) for the keep, bell tower, both lesser towers and the gatehouse, and Z for the long hall, cloister and curtain wall.\n- **Larger files:** keep-drum-b.glb and long-hall.glb are about 1.05 MB each, roughly twice the five smallest, and cloister.glb is 0.8 MB. The difference is almost all textures: those three carry 2048 px maps (798,000, 773,664 and 617,430 bytes of images), the other five 1024 px.\n- **Nothing missing:** no model lacks a texture, and no file holds sound.",
