      "output": "## Land and hand models: checked and handed on unchanged\n\nAll eight files were copied byte for byte and published, and every publish receipt's SHA-256 equals the one the script computed, which also equals the hash supplied with the task.\n\n| File | Bytes | Meshes | Triangles | Materials | Textures (embedded WebP: colour / ORM / normal, bytes) | Size in metres (X × Y × Z) | SHA-256 (first 12) | Same bytes |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|\n| tree-old.glb | 495,400 | 1 | 9,773 | 1 | 3 at 1024 px: 82,052 / 80,802 / 17,542 | 0.990 × 0.838 × 0.998 | `c32f453f2693` | same bytes: yes |\n| pine-scots.glb | 164,300 | 1 | 3,699 | 1 | 3 at 512 px: 39,846 / 17,732 / 2,718 | 0.693 × 0.998 × 0.795 | `7d36c2d42b3e` | same bytes: yes |\n| fir.glb | 154,828 | 1 | 2,174 | 1 | 3 at 512 px: 29,952 / 30,256 / 26,462 | 0.393 × 0.998 × 0.385 | `362488a0d689` | same bytes: yes |\n| boulders.glb | 109,740 | 1 | 1,943 | 1 | 3 at 512 px: 35,986 / 11,972 / 33,394 | 0.951 × 0.658 × 0.996 | `f00bff66e468` | same bytes: yes |\n| rowboat.glb | 90,792 | 1 | 1,956 | 1 | 3 at 512 px: 21,236 / 11,426 / 6,376 | 0.998 × 0.377 × 0.400 | `8388ad5824ae` | same bytes: yes |\n| bench-stone.glb | 73,204 | 1 | 1,714 | 1 | 3 at 512 px: 21,212 / 8,958 / 14,158 | 0.287 × 0.412 × 0.998 | `5536bf373ad7` | same bytes: yes |\n| broom.glb | 354,188 | 1 | 4,192 | 1 | 3 at 1024 px: 110,068 / 55,032 / 84,472 | 0.182 × 0.178 × 0.998 | `cc0179dfd7fc` | same bytes: yes |\n| wand.glb | 32,524 | 1 | 1,184 | 1 | 3 at 256 px: 3,702 / 2,322 / 7,904 | 0.068 × 0.068 × 0.998 | `bf9f72368112` | same bytes: yes |\n\nTotal: 1,474,976 bytes and 26,635 triangles.\n\n- **Compression:** every file lists `EXT_meshopt_compression`, `EXT_texture_webp` and `KHR_mesh_quantization` in both extensionsUsed and extensionsRequired. None uses Draco.\n- **Size:** this is the world box, taken from the POSITION accessor's min and max through the node's scale (0.499; 0.498 for the boulders). Positions are normalised 16-bit integers, so min and max were divided by 32,767 first. The vertex data itself was not decoded.\n- **Structure:** each file has one scene, one node, one mesh with one indexed triangle primitive (POSITION, NORMAL, TEXCOORD_0), and no animations, skins or cameras. The header length equals the file size in all eight.\n- **Checks run:** `inspect_glb.py` (python3, standard library only) reported no problems. `cmp` of each copy against its input found no difference. All eight receipts agreed on the first publish.\n\n**For the builders:**\n- **Loader:** the page's loader must have a meshopt decoder and WebP texture support. All three extensions are required and the uncompressed fallback buffer carries no data, so the models will not load without them.\n- **Scale and axis:** every model is normalised to about 1 m on its longest side and centred on the origin, so the wand is as long as the old tree is wide. The game has to give each its real scale and stand it on the ground. The pine and fir are tall along Y; the broom, wand and bench lie along Z; the boat lies along X.\n- **Largest files:** tree-old.glb is about a third of the set's bytes and triangles (21,095 vertices, three 1024 px textures). In broom.glb, 249,572 of the 354,188 bytes are textures.\n- **Materials:** no model lacks a texture. All materials are opaque, so the foliage is not alpha-cut. The tree, pine, fir, boat and broom are double-sided; the boulders, bench and wand are not. The ORM image is used for metal and roughness only; no occlusion slot is set.\n- **Possible flat normal map:** the pine's normal map is only 2,718 bytes, which suggests it is nearly flat. The image was not decoded, so this is not confirmed.\n- **Sound:** there is no sound in these files.",
